1.6.2: resolver suffix tie-break

'kodachrome_64' was refused as ambiguous because kodachrome_64_generic
contains it - punishing the user for typing a complete stock name.
Substring ties now break toward the single candidate that ends with the
request at an underscore boundary; genuinely ambiguous requests
(e.g. 'kodachrome') still list candidates and refuse. Matrix test
covers both.
